oses linking the groups because the same sonographer collected all measurements. The report includes the distribution checks for analysis.","tutorialEligible":false,"routineEligible":true,"earliestFacilityStage":2,"requiredClinicalSetting":"clinic","requiredCapabilityIds":[],"rewardTierId":"reward.clinic_basic","sourceLabels":["Two-Sample t-Test","Paired t-Test","McNemar Test","ACR Appropriateness Criteria Breast Imaging During Lactation","Academy of Breastfeeding Medicine Clinical Protocol #36: The Mastitis Spectrum, Revised 2022"],"decisionNodes":[{"id":"node.gs028se.independent-t-paired-t.a-two-cohorts.1","questionVariantId":"question.statistics-ethics.independent-t.v2","primaryConceptId":"concept.statistics-ethics.independent-t","stem":"Which analysis best fits the study's comparison of mean remaining abscess-cavity area, using the measurements and assumptions in the exhibit?","answerChoices":[{"id":"correct_two-cohorts","label":"Two-sample t test","isCorrect":true,"rationale":"The study compares means from two groups of different people, and its stated continuous-data assumptions are reasonable. A two-sample t procedure matches that structure.","serviceRequest":null},{"id":"d2_two-cohorts","label":"Wilcoxon rank-sum test","isCorrect":false,"rationale":"Rank-sum answers a ranked-observation comparison. This study explicitly requests means and supplies reasonable assumptions for the mean-based procedure.","serviceRequest":null},{"id":"d3_two-cohorts","label":"Chi-square test of independence","isCorrect":false,"rationale":"Chi-square testing analyzes counts in categories. The requested comparison concerns continuous measurements or ordered ratings, not a categorical contingency table.","serviceRequest":null},{"id":"d1_two-cohorts","label":"Paired t test","isCorrect":false,"rationale":"A paired t procedure needs repeated or deliberately matched measurements. This comparison does not supply those links between observations.","serviceRequest":null}],"shuffleAnswers":