st":null},{"id":"wrong-1-3","label":"Declining enrollment limits access to routine follow-up","isCorrect":false,"rationale":"Limiting routine follow-up uses ordinary care to pressure enrollment. The optional study is not required for that care.","serviceRequest":null},{"id":"key-1","label":"Declining enrollment does not forfeit ordinary care","isCorrect":true,"rationale":"This study is optional and not required for ordinary care. Clarify that declining enrollment does not forfeit that care, so the invitation can be considered voluntarily.","serviceRequest":null}],"shuffleAnswers":true,"explanation":"Clarify that declining this optional study does not forfeit ordinary clinic care. The recruiter's stated condition is inconsistent with voluntary participation in a study not required for that care.","teachingPoint":"Research participation must be voluntary. When a study is optional and not required for ordinary care, declining it should not forfeit that care. Remember to separate the clinical care decision from the research invitation. Making enrollment a condition of routine care pressures the patient instead of supporting an independent choice about participation.","sourceLabels":["Informed Consent in Research","Informed Consent","2023 GEIS Guidelines for gastrointestinal stromal tumors","Gastrointestinal Stromal Tumors Treatment (PDQ®), Health Professional Version"],"resultGateAfter":null,"terminalDispositions":[]},{"id":"node.gs028se.p2e.research-consent.v1.gist.2","questionVariantId":"question.gastric-gist.mutation-guided-neoadjuvant-imatinib.v1.p2e.research-consent.v1","primaryConceptId":"concept.gastric-gist.mutation-guided-neoadjuvant-imatinib","currentUpdate":"The team explains that Colin Lennox's ordinary gastric-GIST care does not depend on joining the optional study. The specialist reviews completed core pathology and molecular testing showing GIST with an imatinib-sensitive mutation and no metastatic disease. The large posterior fundus mass abuts the pancre