","staff.endoscopy_nurse","staff.endoscopist","staff.periop_nurse","staff.surgeon","staff.or_nurse","staff.pharmacist","staff.radiologist"]},"chiefComplaint":"lactational breast abscess study","presentation":"Marley, the breast-service research lead, reviews a trial of a new topical agent after drainage of lactational breast abscesses. Different participants received each preparation. Ultrasound measured the remaining cavity area at the protocol visit. A colleague proposes linking the groups because the same sonographer collected all measurements. The report includes the distribution checks for analysis.","tutorialEligible":false,"routineEligible":true,"earliestFacilityStage":2,"requiredClinicalSetting":"clinic","requiredCapabilityIds":[],"rewardTierId":"reward.clinic_basic","sourceLabels":["Two-Sample t-Test","Paired t-Test","McNemar Test","ACR Appropriateness Criteria Breast Imaging During Lactation","Academy of Breastfeeding Medicine Clinical Protocol #36: The Mastitis Spectrum, Revised 2022"],"decisionNodes":[{"id":"node.gs028se.independent-t-paired-t.a-two-cohorts.1","questionVariantId":"question.statistics-ethics.independent-t.v2","primaryConceptId":"concept.statistics-ethics.independent-t","stem":"Which analysis best fits the study's comparison of mean remaining abscess-cavity area, using the measurements and assumptions in the exhibit?","answerChoices":[{"id":"correct_two-cohorts","label":"Two-sample t test","isCorrect":true,"rationale":"The study compares means from two groups of different people, and its stated continuous-data assumptions are reasonable. A two-sample t procedure matches that structure.","serviceRequest":null},{"id":"d2_two-cohorts","label":"Wilcoxon rank-sum test","isCorrect":false,"rationale":"Rank-sum answers a ranked-observation comparison. This study explicitly requests means and supplies reasonable assumptions for the mean-based procedure.","serviceRequest":null},{"id":"d3_two-cohorts","label":"Chi-square test of independence","isCorr