discussion.employee.0","clinicalReleaseId":"clinical.synthetic.prototype.v1","frozenCase":{"id":"case.gs028se.independent-t-paired-t.a-two-cohorts","displayName":"Select an independent-samples t test and Select a paired t test","patientPresentationVariantId":"presentation.gs028se.independent-t-paired-t.a-two-cohorts","releasePointId":"release.l0.clinic_evaluation","patientDisplayName":"Marley","participant":{"kind":"employee_discussion","requiredStaffRoleDefinitionIds":["staff.glp1_np","staff.endoscopy_nurse","staff.endoscopist","staff.periop_nurse","staff.surgeon","staff.or_nurse","staff.pharmacist","staff.radiologist"]},"chiefComplaint":"lactational breast abscess study","presentation":"Marley, the breast-service research lead, reviews a trial of a new topical agent after drainage of lactational breast abscesses. Different participants received each preparation. Ultrasound measured the remaining cavity area at the protocol visit. A colleague proposes linking the groups because the same sonographer collected all measurements. The report includes the distribution checks for analysis.","tutorialEligible":false,"routineEligible":true,"earliestFacilityStage":2,"requiredClinicalSetting":"clinic","requiredCapabilityIds":[],"rewardTierId":"reward.clinic_basic","sourceLabels":["Two-Sample t-Test","Paired t-Test","McNemar Test","ACR Appropriateness Criteria Breast Imaging During Lactation","Academy of Breastfeeding Medicine Clinical Protocol #36: The Mastitis Spectrum, Revised 2022"],"decisionNodes":[{"id":"node.gs028se.independent-t-paired-t.a-two-cohorts.1","questionVariantId":"question.statistics-ethics.independent-t.v2","primaryConceptId":"concept.statistics-ethics.independent-t","stem":"Which analysis best fits the study's comparison of mean remaining abscess-cavity area, using the measurements and assumptions in the exhibit?","answerChoices":[{"id":"correct_two-cohorts","label":"Two-sample t test","isCorrect":true,"rationale":"The study compares means from two groups of different people, and its stated continuous-data assumptions are reasonable. A two-sample t procedure matches that structure.","serviceRequest":null},{"id":"d2_two-cohorts","label":"Wilcoxon rank-sum test","isCorrect":false,"rationale":"Rank-sum answers a ranked-observation comparison. This study explicitly requests means and supplies reasonable assumptions for the mean-based procedure.","serviceRequest":null},{"id":"d3_two-cohorts","label":"Chi-square test of independence","isCorrect":false,"rationale":"Chi-square testing analyzes counts in categories. The requested comparison concerns continuous measurements or ordered ratings, not a categorical contingency table.","serviceRequest":null},{"id":"d1_two-cohorts","label":"Paired t test","isCorrect":false,"rationale":"A paired t procedure needs repeated or deliberately matched measurements. This comparison does not supply those links between observations.","serviceRequest":null}],"shuffleAnswers":true,"explanation":"A two-sample t test fits mean remaining abscess-cavity area in two nonoverlapping groups. Using the same sonographer does not create repeated or matched observations.","teachingPoint":"The scanner does not define the relationship between observations. These abscess-cavity areas come from different people in two nonoverlapping groups, with suitable continuous-data assumptions. A two-sample t test compares their means. Remember to ask who was measured, not whether the groups used the same instrument or had the same number of columns.","exhibit":{"kind":"abstract","title":"Remaining abscess-cavity area — illustrative clinical study","body":"Invented protocol observations for an unnamed investigational topical agent in lactational breast abscesses. Outcome: remaining abscess-cavity area, in square centimeters. Two separately sampled treatment groups contribute one measurement per person. Groups do not overlap and nobody is matched. Measurements are approximately normal with comparable variability and no influential outliers. These practice assumptions supply no real treatment efficacy."},"sourceLabels":["Two-Sample t-Test","Paired t-Test","McNemar Test","ACR Appropriateness Criteria Breast Imaging During Lactation","Academy of Breastfeeding Medicine Clinical Protocol #36: The Mastitis Spectrum, Revised 2022"],"resultGateAfter":null,"terminalDispositions":[{"answerChoiceId":"d1_two-cohorts","kind":"no_terminal_outcome","consequenceNarrative":"Review the teaching point and choice rationales.","clinicalRationale":"A two-sample t test fits mean remaining abscess-cavity area in two nonoverlapping groups. Using the same sonographer does not create repeated or matched observations.","sourceLabels":["Two-Sample t-Test","Paired t-Test","McNemar Test"]},{"answerChoiceId":"d2_two-cohorts","kind":"no_terminal_outcome","consequenceNarrative":"Review the teaching point and choice rationales.","clinicalRationale":"A two-sample t test fits mean remaining abscess-cavity area in two nonoverlapping groups. Using the same sonographer does not create repeated or matched observations.","sourceLabels":["Two-Sample t-Test","Paired t-Test","McNemar Test"]},{"answerChoiceId":"d3_two-cohorts","kind":"no_terminal_outcome","consequenceNarrative":"Review the teaching point and choice rationales.","clinicalRationale":"A two-sample t test fits mean remaining abscess-cavity area in two nonoverlapping groups. Using the same sonographer does not create repeated or matched observations.","sourceLabels":["Two-Sample t-Test","Paired t-Test","McNemar Test"]}]}],"learningSummary":"Review the teaching points and choice rationales for this encounter."},"employeeId":"employee.m9.reader","employeeDisplayName":"Marley","employeeAppearance":{"version":"pixel-avatar.v1","bodyShape":"average","hairStyle":"none","hairShade":1,"faceStyle":"square","outfitStyle":"plain","outfitShade":2,"accessory":"none","skinTone":2,"headVariant":9,"bodyVariant":9,"roleStyle":"receptionist","stillId":"level3-roster-v2.001"},"lifecycl