e,"rationale":"Addresses potential local residual disease but does not provide regional nodal treatment/staging for this adverse histology.","serviceRequest":null}],"shuffleAnswers":true,"explanation":"An endoscopically removed malignant polyp is not automatically cured by a clear-looking scar. The supplied adverse invasive feature supports discussion of oncologic resection with the regional mesentery. CT-negative nodes do not exclude microscopic disease. Exact bowel extent, especially for a transverse lesion, remains an anatomic operative decision.","teachingPoint":"An endoscopically removed malignant polyp is not automatically cured by a clear-looking scar. The supplied adverse invasive feature supports discussion of oncologic resection with the regional mesentery. CT-negative nodes do not exclude microscopic disease. Exact bowel extent, especially for a transverse lesion, remains an anatomic operative decision.","sourceLabels":["ASCRS Clinical Practice Guidelines for the Management of Colon Cancer","Colon Cancer Treatment (PDQ), Health Professional Version","AI-assisted revision: needs_clinician_review (question-authoring.2026-11-02.v4)","AI-assisted revision: needs_clinician_review (question-authoring.2026-11-02.v5)"],"resultGateAfter":null,"terminalDispositions":[{"answerChoiceId":"choice.qq20261102a.b14.d1","kind":"no_terminal_outcome","consequenceNarrative":"The encounter recorded “Endoscopic full-thickness excision centered on the resection scar”.","clinicalRationale":"Addresses potential local residual disease but does not provide regional nodal treatment/staging for this adverse histology.","sourceLabels":["ASCRS Clinical Practice Guidelines for the Management of Colon Cancer","Colon Cancer Treatment (PDQ), Health Professional Version"]},{"answerChoiceId":"choice.qq20261102a.b14.d2","kind":"no_terminal_outcome","consequenceNarrative":"The encounter recorded “Endoscopic scar surveillance with repeat targeted tissue sampling”.","clinicalRationale":"Overweigh